Phishing
It is an attack where criminals trick victims by claiming to be trusted people through sending malicious links or webs and ending up accessing sensitive information without permission.

Types of phishing
Fake emails- this is when an attacker send malicious links through fake emails to get financial or personal information without permission.
Smishing- hackers send fake sms to targeted individuals phones to get access to their accounts
Spear phishing- attacks are aimed at specific individuals for personal benefits.

Warning signs
•	Messages with urgent deadline
•	Suspicious links
•	Spelling mistakes or illegitimate emails
•	Fake prizes 

Phishing prevention
•	Verify senders email
•	Use strong passwords along with multi factor authentication
•	Avoid clicking unknown links
•	Get security software up to date in your computer

What action to take if you are targeted
•	Stop replying unknown people
•	Dont provide confidential information
•	Report fake account
•	Contact your organization to temporary block your account

Conclusion
Phishing can cause financial loss, data breaches and identity theft. This project can help reduce this.

